description:
FOUND s501b (Opus, 2026-09-30) by a breaking-case probe for #2534.  PRE-EXISTING: main 1bae682b (the base extraction) drops it identically; s501b's #2534 change does not touch it (the embedded decl there has a later string eval, so the new promotion declines and the veto path is today's).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s501b/m4/brk11.pl in the s501b worktree; the file path is inlined):
    use strict; use warnings;
    my $f = "/tmp/x";
    sub outer {
      open(my $h, ">", $f) or die;
      { open(my $h, ">", "$f.2") or die; print $h "inner"; close $h; }
      -s $f;
    }
    print "o ", outer(), " ", -s "$f.2", "\n";
    { open(my $g, ">", "$f.3") or die; sub wg { print $g "g" } sub cg { close $g } }
    wg(); my $x = eval q{ 1 + 1 }; cg();
    print "g ", -s "$f.3", " $x\n";
perl: `o 0 5` / `g 1 2`.  PCL: "PCL: statement dropped at … line 9: ) -- Handle single node of unknown type", "… or die; -- Bug. Fell through. Missing case: []", "… } -- Handle single node …", then the run dies.

MEASURED (bisection, each step one change): removing the two lines containing `.2` (the inner block of `outer` and the print that reads "$f.2") makes it run and agree with perl; removing the anon-sub lines does not; the `$g` block alone with `eval q{}` after it runs (brk6.pl); `sub outer { -s … }` + the `$g` block runs (brk9.pl).  So the trigger needs BOTH the nested same-name `open(my $h` inside a named sub AND the later string eval — suspect the M-F eval-capture registration (_reg_eval_capture / _pending_eval_caps) or _rename_captured_file_lexicals' eval refusal leaving a half-renamed token stream; `PCL_SPAN_DEBUG=1 ./pl2cl` shows the CAPREFUSE lines to start from.  Cheap discriminating measurement: run with `eval q{…}` replaced by `eval { … }` (a block) — if the drop disappears, it is the string-eval arm.

BAR: Pl/ => corpus-diff + the full sweep (a rename/scoping change); a guard row with this shape.
